      ":question/id": "5dfaef1d-ca05-5ac8-a306-4f9a2ea380fd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 4 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $A$ and $C$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(C)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$A$  and $C$ only.\"",
